PURPOSE of misc/guest-poweroff
Description: Verify x86_64 guest successfully powers off
Author: Eddie Kovsky <ekovsky@redhat.com>

Verify x86_64 guest successfully powers off

This test is intended to be used by a host hypervisor to verify that a libvirt
x86_64 guest named "GuestOne" can shut down successfully when the poweroff command
is issued from the host. In order for this test to work correctly the guest
environment must be set up by the test framework. The state of the guest is
deliberately monitored from the host so that the test does not rely on the
guest machine to self-report its running state.
